window.LESSONS=[
{id:'villi',name:'01 Villi 絨毛',title:'Built for absorption · 吸收的適應',doc:'a',page:1,refs:[['a',1],['a',2],['a',4],['a',9],['a',10],['a',11],['a',12],['a',13]],mode:'villi',
text:`<h2>Absorption in small intestine<br><span class="zh">小腸吸收的適應</span></h2><table><thead><tr><th>Adaptation 適應</th><th>Significance 重要性</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Very long 小腸很長</td><td>More time and surface area for absorption.<br>延長吸收時間及增加表面積。</td></tr>
<tr><td>Highly folded wall; numerous villi; microvilli on epithelial cells<br>內壁高度折疊、很多絨毛及微絨毛</td><td>Increase surface area for diffusion and active transport.<br>增加擴散和主動運輸的表面積。</td></tr>
<tr><td>Many mitochondria in epithelial cells<br>上皮細胞有大量線粒體</td><td>Aerobic respiration releases energy (ATP) for active transport.<br>有氧呼吸釋放能量，供主動運輸使用。</td></tr>
<tr><td>One-cell-thick epithelium<br>上皮只有一層細胞厚</td><td>Short diffusion distance for food molecules into blood.<br>縮短食物分子擴散進入血液的距離。</td></tr>
<tr><td>Lacteals and capillary network<br>乳糜管及微血管網</td><td>Rapidly carry absorbed molecules away; maintain a steep concentration gradient and increase diffusion rate.<br>迅速帶走已吸收的分子，維持陡濃度梯度，加快擴散。</td></tr>
<tr><td>Movement of villi through peristalsis<br>蠕動使絨毛移動</td><td>Contact with freshly digested food; maintain a steep concentration gradient.<br>接觸剛消化的食物，維持陡濃度梯度。</td></tr></tbody></table>
<h3>Flattened villi · 扁平的絨毛</h3><div class="flow-line">Surface area ↓ → absorption of digested food ↓ → more food molecules remain in lumen → water potential in lumen ↓ → less water absorbed by osmosis → more water in faeces → diarrhoea 腹瀉。</div>
<p>For micrograph questions, describe <mark>features actually visible</mark> in the image. Use the original exercise diagrams to practise. 顯微照片題只描述可觀察到的特徵。</p>`,
questions:[{q:'Flattened villi cause diarrhoea mainly because… 絨毛扁平導致腹瀉，主要原因是：',options:['More absorbed food raises blood water potential','Unabsorbed solutes lower lumen water potential','Villi begin digesting fibre'],answer:1,explain:'Less absorption leaves more solute in the lumen. Its lower water potential reduces water absorption by osmosis. 吸收減少令腸腔留下更多溶質，水勢下降，水的吸收減少。'}]},
{id:'transport',name:'02 Transport 運輸',title:'Two routes, one circulation · 兩條運輸途徑',doc:'b',page:2,refs:[['a',3],['b',1],['b',2],['b',4],['b',10],['b',11]],mode:'route',
text:`<h2>Transport & assimilation<br><span class="zh">運輸及同化</span></h2><table><thead><tr><th>Water-soluble 水溶性</th><th>Lipid-soluble 脂溶性</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Simple sugars / monosaccharides 單糖<br>Amino acids 氨基酸<br>Minerals 礦物質<br>Vitamins B, C<br>Water 水</td><td>Lipids 脂質<br>Vitamins A, D, E, K</td></tr><tr><td>Capillaries in villi<br>絨毛微血管</td><td>Fatty acids + glycerol recombine into triglycerides in epithelial cells.<br>脂肪酸和甘油在上皮細胞內重組成甘油三酯。<br>→ Lacteals 乳糜管</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatic portal vein 肝門靜脈<br>↓ Liver 肝臟<br>↓ Hepatic vein 肝靜脈<br>↓ Vena cava 腔靜脈</td><td>Lymph vessels 淋巴管<br>↓ Thoracic duct 胸導管<br>↓ Left venous junction 左靜脈角（左鎖骨下靜脈附近）<br>↓ Rejoin blood 重回血液<br>↓ Vena cava 腔靜脈</td></tr><tr><td colspan="2">Heart 心臟 → Aorta 主動脈 → Whole body 全身 → taken up by body cells for use 被身體細胞攝取及利用 [Assimilation 同化]</td></tr></tbody></table><p><mark>Lipids rejoin blood before reaching the heart.</mark><br>脂質在到達心臟前已重回血液。</p><aside class="flow-line"><strong>Route accuracy · 路徑補充</strong><br>Blood returning from the liver enters the inferior vena cava. Lymph joins venous blood near the left subclavian vein, then reaches the superior vena cava. Both enter the right side of the heart → lungs → left side of the heart → aorta. The diagrams omit the lung circuit to focus on nutrition.<br>肝靜脈血經下腔靜脈回心；淋巴在左鎖骨下靜脈附近匯入血液，再經上腔靜脈回心。兩者均先到右心 → 肺 → 左心 → 主動脈。圖中省略肺循環以集中顯示營養運輸。<br>The lipid animation represents most long-chain dietary fat: reassembled triglycerides are packaged in chylomicrons before entering lacteals. Free glycerol and short-chain fatty acids can enter portal blood directly. The original notes retain their course shorthand.<br>脂質動畫代表大部分長鏈膳食脂肪：重組的甘油三酯先包裝成乳糜微粒，再入乳糜管。游離甘油及短鏈脂肪酸可直接進入門靜脈血。原筆記保留課程簡化表述。<br><a href="https://openstax.org/books/anatomy-and-physiology-2e/pages/23-7-chemical-digestion-and-absorption-a-closer-look" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Absorption reference</a> · <a href="https://openstax.org/books/anatomy-and-physiology-2e/pages/23-6-accessory-organs-in-digestion-the-liver-pancreas-and-gallbladder" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Liver reference</a> · <a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/30020599/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Lymph return reference</a></aside><h3>Vessel reminders · 血管提示</h3><p>Arteries carry blood away from the heart; veins return blood towards the heart.<br>動脈把血液帶離心臟；靜脈把血液送回心臟。</p><p>The notes compare systemic arteries (more O₂, less CO₂) and veins (less O₂, more CO₂). 圖中比較體循環的動脈與靜脈。</p>`,
questions:[{q:'Which route is taken by absorbed amino acids? 氨基酸的運輸途徑是：',options:['Lacteal → lymph → heart','Capillaries → hepatic portal vein → liver','Capillaries → hepatic vein → liver'],answer:1,explain:'Amino acids are water-soluble and first enter capillaries, then the hepatic portal vein and liver. 氨基酸屬水溶性，先入微血管，再經肝門靜脈到肝。'}]},
{id:'assimilation',name:'03 Assimilation 同化',title:'Fates of absorbed food · 食物的去向',doc:'b',page:3,refs:[['b',3],['b',7],['b',36],['b',37]],mode:'fates',
text:`<h2>Fates of absorbed food<br><span class="zh">已吸收食物的去向</span></h2><table><thead><tr><th>Nutrient 營養素</th><th>Functions 功能</th><th>When excess 過量時</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Glucose 葡萄糖</td><td>Used for releasing energy.<br>用於釋放能量。</td><td>Converted to glycogen in liver / muscles; or lipids in the liver.<br>轉成肝／肌肉的糖原，或在肝轉成脂質。</td></tr><tr><td>Amino acids 氨基酸</td><td>Make proteins for growth and repair; enzymes, antibodies and hormones.<br>製造蛋白質作生長及修補；製造酶、抗體和激素。</td><td>Deaminated in liver.<br>Amino group → urea → excreted in urine.<br>Remaining parts → glucose / glycogen / lipids.<br>在肝脫氨；氨基部分形成尿素，隨尿排出；其餘部分轉成葡萄糖、糖原或脂質。</td></tr><tr><td>Lipids 脂質</td><td>Energy storage; make cell membranes and sex hormones.<br>儲存能量；製造細胞膜及性激素。</td><td>Deposited around internal organs; stored in adipose tissue, e.g. subcutaneous fat.<br>沉積於內臟周圍和脂肪組織，如皮下脂肪。</td></tr></tbody></table><h3>Three different processes · 三個不同過程</h3><div class="flow-line">Digestion 消化 → large molecules broken into small molecules.<br>Absorption 吸收 → digested molecules enter blood / lymph.<br>Assimilation 同化 → body cells take up absorbed molecules for use.</div><p class="badge">The model follows the simplified routes and fates in these notes. 模型依照本筆記的課程表述。</p>`,
questions:[{q:'What happens to excess amino acids? 過量氨基酸會怎樣？',options:['Stored unchanged in a special amino-acid store','Deaminated in the liver; nitrogenous part forms urea','Egested through the anus'],answer:1,explain:'The liver deaminates excess amino acids. Urea is excreted in urine; remaining parts can form glucose, glycogen or lipids. 肝進行脫氨作用，尿素隨尿排出，其餘部分可轉成葡萄糖、糖原或脂質。'}]},
{id:'glucose',name:'04 Blood glucose 血糖',title:'Meal, fasting and the liver · 餐後與飢餓',doc:'b',page:7,refs:[['b',2],['b',3],['b',7],['b',9],['b',12],['b',13],['b',14],['b',17],['b',23]],mode:'glucose',
text:`<h2>Blood glucose regulation<br><span class="zh">血糖調節與血管比較</span></h2><table><thead><tr><th>Situation 情況</th><th>Response 反應</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>After carbohydrate meal / sugary drink<br>進食碳水化合物／含糖飲品後</td><td>Blood glucose rises → insulin increases → liver converts glucose into glycogen → liver glycogen increases → blood glucose returns towards normal.<br>血糖升高 → 胰島素增加 → 肝將葡萄糖轉成糖原 → 肝糖原增加 → 血糖回復正常水平。</td></tr><tr><td>Starvation / fasting<br>飢餓／空腹</td><td>Low blood glucose → less insulin, more glucagon → liver glycogen breaks down to glucose → glucose released into hepatic vein.<br>低血糖 → 胰島素減少、升糖素增加 → 肝糖原分解成葡萄糖 → 葡萄糖進入肝靜脈。</td></tr><tr><td>High-protein diet<br>高蛋白飲食</td><td>Excess amino acids → liver deamination → more urea in hepatic vein.<br>過量氨基酸 → 肝脫氨 → 肝靜脈尿素增加。</td></tr></tbody></table><h3>After a meal · 餐後比較</h3><table><thead><tr><th>Contents 成分</th><th>Hepatic portal vein 肝門靜脈</th><th>Hepatic vein 肝靜脈</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Glucose 葡萄糖</td><td>More 較多</td><td>Less 較少</td></tr><tr><td>Amino acids 氨基酸</td><td>More 較多</td><td>Less 較少</td></tr><tr><td>Urea 尿素</td><td>Less 較少</td><td>More 較多</td></tr><tr><td>O₂ 氧</td><td>Higher 較高</td><td>Lower 較低</td></tr><tr><td>CO₂ 二氧化碳</td><td>Lower 較低</td><td>Higher 較高</td></tr></tbody></table><p><mark>The comparison changes with the situation.</mark> During starvation, the hepatic vein carries the highest glucose concentration among the vessels in the notes' questions.<br>血管比較取決於情況；飢餓時，題目所列血管中肝靜脈的葡萄糖濃度最高。</p>`,
questions:[{q:'During starvation, which vessel in the notes has the highest glucose content? 飢餓時哪條血管的葡萄糖含量最高？',options:['Hepatic portal vein 肝門靜脈','Hepatic vein 肝靜脈','Hepatic artery 肝動脈'],answer:1,explain:'Glucagon promotes liver glycogen breakdown. Glucose leaves the liver in the hepatic vein. 升糖素促進肝糖原分解，葡萄糖經肝靜脈離開肝臟。'}]},
{id:'liver',name:'05 Liver 肝臟',title:'The liver at work · 肝臟的功能',doc:'b',page:3,refs:[['b',3],['b',7],['b',8],['b',12],['b',14],['b',31],['b',36],['b',37]],mode:'liver',
text:`<h2>Liver functions<br><span class="zh">肝臟的功能</span></h2><table><thead><tr><th>Function 類別</th><th>Details 詳情</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Regulating 調節</td><td>Glucose → glycogen with increased insulin, lowering blood glucose.<br>Glycogen → glucose with increased glucagon, raising blood glucose.<br>胰島素增加促進葡萄糖轉成糖原，降低血糖；升糖素增加促進糖原轉成葡萄糖，提高血糖。</td></tr><tr><td>Storing 儲存</td><td>Glycogen; iron from red blood cell breakdown; fat-soluble vitamins A, D, E, K.<br>糖原、紅血球分解所得的鐵、脂溶性維生素。</td></tr><tr><td>Producing 生產</td><td>Bile; vitamin A from carotene.<br>膽汁；將胡蘿蔔素轉成維生素 A。</td></tr><tr><td>Deaminating 脫氨</td><td>Excess amino acids → urea (nitrogenous part).<br>過量氨基酸的含氮部分轉成尿素。</td></tr><tr><td>Detoxifying 解毒</td><td>Process mildly toxic substances; catalase breaks down hydrogen peroxide.<br>處理輕度有毒物質；過氧化氫酶分解過氧化氫。</td></tr></tbody></table><h3>Why does oral insulin not work?<br>為何口服胰島素無效？</h3><p>Insulin is a protein. Digestive enzymes break it down before it can act as an intact hormone.<br>胰島素是蛋白質，會被消化酶分解，不能以完整激素發揮作用。</p><h3>Bile & gall bladder · 膽汁與膽囊</h3><p>Liver produces bile; gall bladder stores it. Bile salts emulsify fat into small droplets, increasing surface area for lipase. Alkaline bile helps neutralize acidic chyme.<br>肝製造膽汁，膽囊儲存膽汁。膽鹽乳化脂肪，增加脂肪酶作用的表面積；鹼性膽汁協助中和酸性食糜。</p><p>After gall bladder removal, bile enters the duodenum directly; its amount / concentration may be insufficient for effective emulsification of a fatty meal, as discussed in the supplied answer.<br>切除膽囊後，膽汁直接流入十二指腸；筆記答案指出其份量／濃度可能不足以有效乳化脂肪。</p>`,
questions:[{q:'Which is produced by the liver? 哪項由肝臟製造？',options:['Bile 膽汁','Insulin 胰島素','Pancreatic lipase 胰脂肪酶'],answer:0,explain:'The liver makes bile; the gall bladder stores it. Insulin and pancreatic lipase are produced by the pancreas. 肝製造膽汁，膽囊儲存膽汁；胰島素及胰脂肪酶由胰製造。'}]},
{id:'egestion',name:'06 Egestion 排遺',title:'Large intestine & egestion · 大腸與排遺',doc:'b',page:18,refs:[['b',18],['b',19],['b',20],['b',21],['b',22],['b',23],['b',24],['b',25],['b',26]],mode:'egestion',
text:`<h2>Large intestine & egestion<br><span class="zh">大腸與排遺</span></h2><div class="flow-line">Colon 結腸 → absorbs water 吸收水分 → contents become more solid 內容物變得較固體 → faeces 糞便 → rectum 直腸 stores faeces → anus 肛門 → egestion 排遺。</div><table><thead><tr><th>Egestion 排遺</th><th>Excretion 排泄</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Removal of undigested / unabsorbed material in faeces through the anus.<br>未消化／未吸收物質以糞便經肛門排出。</td><td>Removal of metabolic waste produced by cells, e.g. urea in urine.<br>排出細胞代謝產生的廢物，例如尿中的尿素。</td></tr></tbody></table><h3>Faeces · 糞便成分</h3><p>Unabsorbed residues including insoluble dietary fibre, bacteria and water. Insoluble fibre in spinach is undigested and unabsorbed, so it is egested.<br>包括不溶性膳食纖維的未吸收殘餘物、細菌和水。菠菜中的不溶性纖維不被消化或吸收，經排遺離開身體。</p><h3>Bile pigment route · 膽色素的路徑</h3><div class="flow-line">Liver 肝 → gall bladder 膽囊 → bile duct 膽管 → duodenum 十二指腸 → ileum 迴腸 → large intestine 大腸 → anus 肛門。</div><h3>Use the original figures · 配合原圖</h3><p>Open the linked source pages for sphincter locations, the alimentary canal, muscles, digestion summaries, and the obesity surgery question. All original diagrams and question labels are retained.<br>相關頁面保留括約肌位置、消化道、肌肉、消化總結及肥胖手術題的全部原圖及標示。</p>`,
questions:[{q:'Undigested insoluble fibre leaves the body by… 不溶性纖維經哪個過程離開身體？',options:['Assimilation 同化','Excretion 排泄','Egestion 排遺'],answer:2,explain:'Insoluble fibre is undigested and unabsorbed; it passes out in faeces through the anus. 不溶性纖維未被消化或吸收，隨糞便經肛門排出。'}]},
{id:'applications',name:'07 Applications 應用',title:'Apply the mechanisms · 應用與實驗',doc:'a',page:8,refs:[['a',8],['a',9],['a',12],['a',13],['a',14],['a',19],['a',20],['a',26],['a',27],['a',28],['a',29],['b',32]],mode:'application',
text:`<h2>Transport, disease & experiments<br><span class="zh">運輸、疾病與實驗</span></h2><table><thead><tr><th>Process 過程</th><th>Direction & energy 方向與能量</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Diffusion 擴散</td><td>High → low concentration, towards equilibrium; no metabolic energy required.<br>高濃度至低濃度，直至平衡；不需代謝能量。</td></tr><tr><td>Osmosis 滲透</td><td>Water across a selectively permeable membrane; higher → lower water potential (less → more solute).<br>水經選擇透性膜，由高水勢至低水勢，即由較少溶質至較多溶質。</td></tr><tr><td>Active transport 主動運輸</td><td>Requires energy in living cells; can absorb against the concentration gradient.<br>活細胞需用能量，可逆濃度梯度吸收。</td></tr></tbody></table><h3>Coeliac disease · 乳糜瀉</h3><p>Gluten triggers an immune response damaging and flattening villi → smaller absorption surface → malabsorption and nutrient deficiency. Use the source questions for symptoms, evidence, and experimental comparisons.<br>麩質引發免疫反應，損害並壓平絨毛 → 吸收面積減少 → 吸收不良及營養缺乏。原題保留症狀、證據及實驗比較。</p><h3>Lactose intolerance · 乳糖不耐症</h3><div class="flow-line">Insufficient lactase 乳糖酶不足 → lactose not digested into glucose + galactose → lactose remains in intestine → water potential ↓ → water absorption ↓ → more water in faeces / diarrhoea。</div><p>Lactase is embedded in small-intestine epithelial cell membranes. After digestion, monosaccharides enter villus capillaries and travel to the liver for processing or glycogen storage.<br>乳糖酶位於小腸上皮細胞膜。消化所得的單糖進入微血管，到肝處理或轉成糖原。</p><p>Calcium supports bones and teeth, blood clotting and muscle contraction. The supplied answer lists almonds, broccoli and fish as alternative sources.<br>鈣參與骨骼及牙齒形成、凝血與肌肉收縮。筆記答案列出杏仁、西蘭花及魚等其他來源。</p><h3>Lipase practical · 脂肪酶實驗</h3><p>Lipase forms fatty acids and glycerol; fatty acids lower pH. Bile salts emulsify fat into smaller droplets, increasing surface area and speeding lipase action. Read the original experimental graphs, tables, conditions and marking points in the source pages.<br>脂肪酶產生脂肪酸和甘油，脂肪酸令 pH 下降。膽鹽乳化脂肪，增大表面積，加快脂肪酶作用。原頁保留所有實驗圖表、條件及評分點。</p>`,
questions:[{q:'Why do bile salts speed up lipase action? 為何膽鹽能加快脂肪酶的作用？',options:['They digest lipids into amino acids','They increase lipid surface area by emulsification','They are themselves lipase enzymes'],answer:1,explain:'Emulsification makes small droplets with a larger total surface area for lipase. 乳化形成細小油滴，增加脂肪酶作用的總表面積。'}]}
];
